{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "```python\ndef remove_Occ(input_string: str, target_char: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes the first and last occurrences of a target character from a string.\n    Returns the original string if the character is not found.\"\"\"\n    first_idx = input_string.find(target_char)\n    last_idx = input_string.rfind(target_char)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return input_string\n    elif first_idx == last_idx:\n        # Character appears only once\n        return input_string[:first_idx] + input_string[first_idx + 1:]\n    else:\n        # Character appears multiple times\n        return input_string[:first_idx] + \\\n               input_string[first_idx + 1 : last_idx] + \\\n               input_string[last_idx + 1:]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/12", "solution": "```python\nimport typing\n\ndef sort_matrix(matrix: typing.List[typing.List[typing.Union[int, float]]]) -> typing.List[typing.List[typing.Union[int, float]]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a matrix by the sum of its rows in ascending order.\n    Returns a new matrix with rows reordered based on their sums.\n    \"\"\"\n    rows_with_sums = []\n    for row in matrix:\n        row_sum = sum(row)\n        rows_with_sums.append((row_sum, row))\n\n    rows_with_sums.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n\n    sorted_matrix = [row for _, row in rows_with_sums]\n    return sorted_matrix\n```"}
