{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "```python\ndef remove_Occ(input_string: str, char_to_remove: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes the first and last occurrences of a specified character from a string.\n    Returns the modified string with the first and last occurrences of the character removed.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_string or not char_to_remove or len(char_to_remove) != 1:\n        return input_string\n\n    first_idx = input_string.find(char_to_remove)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return input_string\n\n    last_idx = input_string.rfind(char_to_remove)\n\n    if first_idx == last_idx:\n        return input_string[:first_idx] + input_string[first_idx+1:]\n\n    # Reconstruct the string by removing both occurrences from the original string.\n    result_string = input_string[:first_idx] + input_string[first_idx+1:last_idx] + input_string[last_idx+1:]\n\n    return result_string\n```"}
