{"task_id": "Mbpp/3", "solution": "```python\ndef is_not_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a number is not prime.\n    Returns True if n is not prime (i.e., n <= 1 or n is composite), False if n is prime.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n    if n == 2:\n        return False\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        return True\n\n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= n:\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return True\n        i += 2\n    return False\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/3", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef is_not_prime(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given integer is not a prime number based on defined rules.\n    Returns True if the number is not prime, False otherwise.\"\"\"\n    if number <= 1:\n        return True\n    if number == 2:\n        return False\n    if number % 2 == 0:  # Covers even numbers greater than 2\n        return True\n\n    # For odd numbers greater than 2\n    # Iterate from 3 up to the square root of the number, with a step of 2\n    for divisor in range(3, int(math.isqrt(number)) + 1, 2):\n        if number % divisor == 0:\n            return True\n\n    return False\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/18", "solution": "```python\ndef remove_dirty_chars(source_string: str, dirty_chars_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes characters from the first string which are present in the second string.\n    Returns a new string with the specified characters removed.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not source_string:\n        return \"\"\n    if not dirty_chars_string:\n        return source_string\n\n    # Convert dirty_chars_string to a set for efficient O(1) average-case lookup.\n    dirty_chars_set = set(dirty_chars_string)\n\n    result_chars = []\n    for char in source_string:\n        if char not in dirty_chars_set:\n            result_chars.append(char)\n\n    return \"\".join(result_chars)\n```"}
