{"task_id": "Mbpp/61", "solution": "```python\ndef count_Substrings(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts substrings where the sum of digits equals their length.\n    Returns 0 for an empty input string.\"\"\"\n    if not input_string:\n        return 0\n\n    total_count = 0\n    n = len(input_string)\n\n    # Iterate through all possible starting indices for substrings\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_sum = 0\n        # Iterate through all possible ending indices from the current start\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            # The current substring is input_string[i:j+1]\n            # Calculate the sum of digits for the current substring incrementally\n            current_sum += int(input_string[j])\n\n            # Calculate the length of the current substring\n            substring_length = (j - i) + 1\n\n            # Check if the sum of digits equals the substring's length\n            if current_sum == substring_length:\n                total_count += 1\n\n    return total_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/63", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Union\n\ndef max_difference(tuple_list: List[Tuple[Union[int, float], Union[int, float]]]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum absolute difference between two numbers in each tuple.\n    Returns the largest difference as an integer, or 0 if the input list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not tuple_list:\n        return 0\n\n    max_diff = 0.0\n\n    for a, b in tuple_list:\n        current_diff = abs(a - b)\n        if current_diff > max_diff:\n            max_diff = current_diff\n\n    return int(max_diff)\n```"}
