{"task_id": "Mbpp/68", "solution": "```python\ndef is_Monotonic(arr: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if an array is monotonic (either increasing or decreasing).\n    An array with zero or one element is considered monotonic.\"\"\"\n\n    if len(arr) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    is_increasing = True\n    is_decreasing = True\n\n    for i in range(len(arr) - 1):\n        if arr[i] > arr[i+1]:\n            is_increasing = False\n        if arr[i] < arr[i+1]:\n            is_decreasing = False\n\n        # If the array is neither increasing nor decreasing at any point, it's not monotonic.\n        if not is_increasing and not is_decreasing:\n            return False\n\n    return is_increasing or is_decreasing\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "```python\ndef bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Bell number B(n) for a given non-negative integer n.\n    The Bell number B(n) is the number of ways to partition a set of n elements.\n\n    Args:\n        n: A non-negative integer.\n\n    Returns:\n        The Bell number B(n).\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If n is a negative integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be an integer.\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize a 2D list for the Bell triangle to compute B(n).\n    # bell_triangle[i][j] represents the number of partitions of a set\n    # with i elements into j non-empty subsets (Stirling numbers of the second kind),\n    # and bell_triangle[i][0] stores the Bell number B(i).\n    bell_triangle = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case: B(0) = 1 (There is one way to partition an empty set: into one empty set)\n    bell_triangle[0][0] = 1\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # The first element of each row is the last element of the previous row.\n        # This is because B(n) = sum_{k=0}^{n-1} C(n-1, k) B(k)\n        # or, more simply using the Bell triangle construction:\n        # B_i = S(i,0) + S(i,1) + ... + S(i,i), where S(i,j) are Stirling numbers of the second kind.\n        # The recurrence relation for Stirling numbers of the second kind is:\n        # S(n, k) = S(n-1, k-1) + k * S(n-1, k)\n        # And for the Bell triangle:\n        # T(n, 0) = T(n-1, n-1)\n        # T(n, k) = T(n-1, k-1) + T(n, k-1)\n        # where T(n, 0) is B(n)\n        bell_triangle[i][0] = bell_triangle[i - 1][i - 1]\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            bell_triangle[i][j] = bell_triangle[i - 1][j - 1] + bell_triangle[i][j - 1]\n\n    # The Bell number B(n) is the first element of the nth row (0-indexed).\n    return bell_triangle[n][0]\n```"}
