{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Any\n\ndef is_samepatterns(sequence: List[Any], patterns: List[Any]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the sequence array follows the pattern defined by the patterns array.\n    This function establishes and verifies a consistent one-to-one mapping.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(sequence) != len(patterns):\n        return False\n\n    pattern_to_seq_map = {}\n    seq_to_pattern_map = {}\n\n    for i in range(len(patterns)):\n        s_char = sequence[i]\n        p_char = patterns[i]\n\n        # Check consistency for pattern_to_seq_map\n        if p_char in pattern_to_seq_map:\n            if pattern_to_seq_map[p_char] != s_char:\n                return False\n        else:\n            pattern_to_seq_map[p_char] = s_char\n\n        # Check consistency for seq_to_pattern_map\n        if s_char in seq_to_pattern_map:\n            if seq_to_pattern_map[s_char] != p_char:\n                return False\n        else:\n            seq_to_pattern_map[s_char] = p_char\n\n    return True\n```"}
