{"task_id": "Mbpp/71", "solution": "```python\ndef comb_sort(list_of_numbers):\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of numerical elements using the Comb Sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new list with elements sorted in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(list_of_numbers)\n    # Create a shallow copy to ensure the original list is not modified.\n    arr = list_of_numbers[:]\n\n    gap = n\n    shrink_factor = 1.3\n    swapped = True\n\n    while gap > 1 or swapped:\n        # Calculate the new gap value.\n        gap = int(gap / shrink_factor)\n        if gap < 1:\n            gap = 1\n\n        swapped = False\n        # Perform a \"bubble sort\" pass for the current gap.\n        for i in range(n - gap):\n            if arr[i] > arr[i + gap]:\n                arr[i], arr[i + gap] = arr[i + gap], arr[i]\n                swapped = True\n    return arr\n```"}
