{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "```python\ndef sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence.\n\n    The Newman-Conway sequence is defined as:\n    P(1) = 1\n    P(2) = 1\n    P(n) = P(P(n-1)) + P(n-P(n-1)) for n > 2\n\n    Args:\n        n: The positive integer representing the desired term in the sequence.\n\n    Returns:\n        The nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    memo = {1: 1, 2: 1}\n\n    def _calculate_nth_term(k: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Helper function to calculate the kth term of the Newman-Conway sequence using memoization.\n        \"\"\"\n        if k in memo:\n            return memo[k]\n\n        # Ensure k remains positive during recursive calls, although sequence definition implies it will.\n        # This check provides robustness against unexpected intermediate values.\n        if k <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid term index encountered: {k}. Sequence terms must be positive.\")\n\n        p_k_minus_1 = _calculate_nth_term(k - 1)\n        term1 = _calculate_nth_term(p_k_minus_1)\n        term2 = _calculate_nth_term(k - p_k_minus_1)\n\n        result = term1 + term2\n        memo[k] = result\n        return result\n\n    return _calculate_nth_term(n)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "```python\ndef sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence.\n    The sequence is defined as P(1)=1, P(2)=1, and P(n)=P(P(n-1))+P(n-P(n-1)) for n > 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 1 or n == 2:\n        return 1\n    return sequence(sequence(n - 1)) + sequence(n - sequence(n - 1))\n```"}
