{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "```python\n_bell_cache = {0: 1}\n_last_bell_triangle_row = [1] # Stores the elements of the last completed row A[k]\n_max_bell_triangle_row_index = 0 # Corresponds to k for _last_bell_triangle_row\n\ndef _calculate_bell_triangle(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes Bell numbers from the last cached index up to n using Aitken's array, populating _bell_cache.\n    It updates a module-level variable to store the last row of the Bell triangle for efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    global _last_bell_triangle_row, _max_bell_triangle_row_index\n\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Bell number is not defined for negative inputs.\")\n    if n <= _max_bell_triangle_row_index:\n        return _bell_cache[n]\n\n    current_row_elements = list(_last_bell_triangle_row)\n    for i in range(_max_bell_triangle_row_index + 1, n + 1):\n        new_row_start_element = current_row_elements[-1]\n        _bell_cache[i] = new_row_start_element\n\n        prev_row_elements = current_row_elements\n        current_row_elements = [new_row_start_element]\n\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            current_row_elements.append(current_row_elements[j-1] + prev_row_elements[j-1])\n\n    _last_bell_triangle_row = current_row_elements\n    _max_bell_triangle_row_index = n\n    return _bell_cache[n]\n\ndef bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number. It uses a cached Bell triangle method for efficiency.\n\n    Args:\n        n (int): The index of the Bell number to calculate. Must be a non-negative integer.\n\n    Returns:\n        int: The nth Bell number.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If n is not an integer.\n        ValueError: If n is a negative integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Bell number is not defined for negative inputs.\")\n\n    if n in _bell_cache:\n        return _bell_cache[n]\n\n    return _calculate_bell_triangle(n)\n```"}
