{"task_id": "Mbpp/96", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef divisor(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of divisors for a given positive integer n.\n    Assumes n is a positive integer as per the problem constraints.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(1, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            if i * i == n:\n                count += 1\n            else:\n                count += 2\n    return count\n```"}
