{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "```python\ndef eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the Eulerian number a(n, m).\n    Applies base cases: a(n, 0) = 1, a(n, m) = 0 if m >= n; otherwise uses recurrence a(n, m) = (m + 1) * a(n - 1, m) + (n - m) * a(n - 1, m - 1).\"\"\"\n    if m == 0:\n        return 1\n    if m >= n:\n        return 0\n\n    return (m + 1) * eulerian_num(n - 1, m) + (n - m) * eulerian_num(n - 1, m - 1)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "```python\ndef eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the Eulerian number a(n, m).\n    Uses dynamic programming with memoization based on recurrence relation.\n    \"\"\"\n    if m < 0 or m >= n:\n        return 0\n    if n == 0 and m == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores A(i, j). Table size (n+1) x (n+1) for convenience.\n    dp = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case: A(0, 0) = 1\n    dp[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table using the recurrence relation\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):  # Iterate for 'n' from 1 to N\n        for j in range(i):  # Iterate for 'm' from 0 to i-1\n            # Recurrence: A(i, j) = (j + 1) * A(i-1, j) + (i - j) * A(i-1, j-1)\n\n            # First term: (j + 1) * A(i-1, j)\n            term1 = (j + 1) * dp[i-1][j]\n\n            # Second term: (i - j) * A(i-1, j-1)\n            term2 = 0\n            if j - 1 >= 0: # Ensure j-1 is a valid index for m\n                term2 = (i - j) * dp[i-1][j-1]\n\n            dp[i][j] = term1 + term2\n\n    return dp[n][m]\n```"}
