{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "```python\ndef common_in_nested_lists(nested_list: list[list[any]]) -> list[any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies and returns elements common to all sub-lists within a given list of lists.\n    This function utilizes set intersections for efficient processing.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nested_list:\n        return []\n\n    # Initialize common_set with elements from the first sub-list.\n    # If the first sub-list is empty, common_set will be empty, leading to an empty result.\n    common_set = set(nested_list[0])\n\n    # Iterate through subsequent sub-lists, updating common_set with intersections.\n    for sub_list in nested_list[1:]:\n        common_set = common_set.intersection(set(sub_list))\n        if not common_set:  # Optimization: if no common elements remain, further checks are unnecessary.\n            break\n\n    # Convert the final set of common elements back to a list.\n    return list(common_set)\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "```python\ndef odd_Equivalent(binary_string: str, num_rotations: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the count of odd decimal values from binary string rotations.\n    It rotates the string `num_rotations` times and checks each decimal equivalent.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_count = 0\n\n    current_string = binary_string\n    for _ in range(num_rotations):\n        # Perform cyclic rotation: move the first character to the end\n        current_string = current_string[1:] + current_string[0]\n\n        # Convert the rotated string to its decimal value\n        decimal_value = int(current_string, 2)\n\n        # Check if the decimal value is odd and increment count if it is\n        if decimal_value % 2 != 0:\n            odd_count += 1\n\n    return odd_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "```python\ndef _rotate_binary_string(binary_str: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Rotates a binary string once to the left.\"\"\"\n    return binary_str[1:] + binary_str[0]\n\ndef _binary_to_decimal(binary_str: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Converts a binary string to its decimal integer equivalent.\"\"\"\n    return int(binary_str, 2)\n\ndef _is_odd(decimal_val: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given decimal integer is odd.\"\"\"\n    return decimal_val % 2 == 1\n\ndef odd_Equivalent(binary_string: str, num_rotations: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of odd decimal values obtained by rotating a binary string.\n    The function performs a specified number of left rotations and counts odd results.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_count = 0\n    current_binary_string = binary_string\n\n    for _ in range(num_rotations):\n        current_binary_string = _rotate_binary_string(current_binary_string)\n        decimal_value = _binary_to_decimal(current_binary_string)\n        if _is_odd(decimal_value):\n            odd_count += 1\n\n    return odd_count\n```"}
