{"task_id": "Mbpp/119", "solution": "def search(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the unique element in a sorted array where all other elements appear twice.\n    The input array is guaranteed to be sorted and follow the pattern.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    # Iterate through the array taking steps of 2, comparing pairs.\n    for i in range(0, n - 1, 2):\n        # If a pair is not equal, the first element of the pair is the unique one.\n        if arr[i] != arr[i + 1]:\n            return arr[i]\n\n    # If the loop completes, the unique element must be the last one in the array.\n    return arr[n - 1]"}
