{"task_id": "Mbpp/123", "solution": "import math\n\ndef _calculate_proper_divisor_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of proper divisors of a given integer n.\n    Proper divisors are positive divisors excluding the number itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return 0\n\n    divisor_sum = 1  # 1 is always a proper divisor for n > 1\n    for i in range(2, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            divisor_sum += i\n            if i * i != n:  # If i is not sqrt(n), add its pair n/i\n                divisor_sum += n // i\n    return divisor_sum\n\ndef amicable_numbers_sum(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all amicable numbers up to a specified limit.\n    It identifies amicable pairs (a, b) where sum_divisors(a) = b and sum_divisors(b) = a, with a != b.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    found_amicable_numbers = set()\n\n    for n in range(1, number + 1):\n        if n in found_amicable_numbers:\n            continue\n\n        sum_div_n = _calculate_proper_divisor_sum(n)\n\n        # Check for potential amicable partner: sum_div_n must be > n and within the limit.\n        if sum_div_n > n and sum_div_n <= number:\n            sum_div_sum_div_n = _calculate_proper_divisor_sum(sum_div_n)\n\n            # Confirm if n and sum_div_n form an amicable pair.\n            if sum_div_sum_div_n == n:\n                total_sum += n\n                total_sum += sum_div_n\n                found_amicable_numbers.add(n)\n                found_amicable_numbers.add(sum_div_n)\n\n    return total_sum```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/123", "solution": "```python\ndef _sum_proper_divisors(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of proper divisors for a given number n.\n    Returns 0 for n=1, and 1 for prime numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    total = 1  # 1 is always a proper divisor for n > 1\n    for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            total += i\n            if i * i != n:\n                total += n // i\n    return total\n\ndef amicable_numbers_sum(limit: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all amicable numbers from 1 to a specified limit.\n    It iterates numbers, finds their proper divisor sums, and identifies amicable pairs.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    found_amicable_numbers = set()\n\n    for a in range(1, limit + 1):\n        if a in found_amicable_numbers:\n            continue\n\n        sum_div_a = _sum_proper_divisors(a)\n\n        # Check conditions for a potential amicable pair\n        if sum_div_a > a and sum_div_a <= limit:\n            sum_div_b = _sum_proper_divisors(sum_div_a)\n\n            if sum_div_b == a:\n                # Found an amicable pair (a, sum_div_a)\n                found_amicable_numbers.add(a)\n                found_amicable_numbers.add(sum_div_a)\n\n    total_sum = sum(found_amicable_numbers)\n    return total_sum\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/126", "solution": "```python\ndef sum(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all common divisors for two given integer numbers.\n    It returns the sum by iterating through possible divisors up to the minimum of the absolute inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    common_divisors_sum = 0\n    limit = min(abs(num1), abs(num2)) # Find the smaller of the two numbers to limit the search for divisors.\n\n    for i in range(1, limit + 1):\n        if num1 % i == 0 and num2 % i == 0:\n            common_divisors_sum += i\n\n    return common_divisors_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/125", "solution": "```python\ndef find_length(binary_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum difference between \\'0\\'s and \\'1\\'s in any substring.\n    Applies a modified Kadane\\'s algorithm to find this maximum difference.\"\"\"\n\n    # Validate that the input string contains only '0's and '1's.\n    for char in binary_string:\n        if char != '0' and char != '1':\n            raise ValueError(\"Input string must contain only '0's and '1's.\")\n\n    max_diff = 0\n    current_diff = 0\n\n    for char in binary_string:\n        if char == '0':\n            current_diff += 1\n        else:  # char == '1'\n            current_diff -= 1\n\n        # If current_diff becomes negative, it means '1's have outnumbered '0's\n        # in the current sequence. Reset to 0 to start a new potential max sequence.\n        if current_diff < 0:\n            current_diff = 0\n\n        # Update overall maximum difference\n        max_diff = max(max_diff, current_diff)\n\n    return max_diff\n```"}
