{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "def _flip(arr, i):\n    \"\"\"Reverses elements of the list 'arr' from index 0 up to 'i' (inclusive).\"\"\"\n    start = 0\n    while start < i:\n        arr[start], arr[i] = arr[i], arr[start]\n        start += 1\n        i -= 1\n\ndef _find_max_index(arr, n):\n    \"\"\"Finds the index of the maximum element within the first 'n' elements of 'arr'.\"\"\"\n    max_val = arr[0]\n    max_idx = 0\n    for j in range(1, n):\n        if arr[j] > max_val:\n            max_val = arr[j]\n            max_idx = j\n    return max_idx\n\ndef pancake_sort(input_list):\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of integers in ascending order using the pancake sort algorithm.\"\"\"\n    arr = list(input_list) # Create a mutable copy to avoid modifying the original list\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    for curr_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find the index of the maximum element in the current unsorted sublist\n        max_idx = _find_max_index(arr, curr_size)\n\n        # Move the maximum element to the end of the current unsorted sublist\n        if max_idx != curr_size - 1:\n            # Flip the sublist up to max_idx to bring the max element to the front\n            _flip(arr, max_idx)\n            # Flip the entire current unsorted sublist to move the max element to its final position\n            _flip(arr, curr_size - 1)\n\n    return arr"}
