{"task_id": "Mbpp/160", "solution": "```python\ndef _extended_gcd(a: int, b: int) -> tuple[int, int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes gcd(a, b) and coefficients x, y such that ax + by = gcd(a, b).\n    This function implements the Extended Euclidean Algorithm recursively.\n    \"\"\"\n    if a == 0:\n        return (b, 0, 1)\n\n    gcd, x1, y1 = _extended_gcd(b % a, a)\n\n    x = y1 - (b // a) * x1\n    y = x1\n\n    return (gcd, x, y)\n\ndef find_solution(a: int, b: int, n: int) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds integer solutions (x, y) for the linear Diophantine equation ax + by = n.\n    Returns (x, y) if an integer solution exists, otherwise None.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Handle edge cases where a or b are zero\n    if a == 0 and b == 0:\n        return (0, 0) if n == 0 else None\n\n    if a == 0:\n        return (0, n // b) if n % b == 0 else None\n\n    if b == 0:\n        return (n // a, 0) if n % a == 0 else None\n\n    # Determine original signs for coefficient adjustment later\n    sign_a = 1 if a >= 0 else -1\n    sign_b = 1 if b >= 0 else -1\n\n    # Apply Extended Euclidean Algorithm to absolute values of a and b\n    gcd_val, x0, y0 = _extended_gcd(abs(a), abs(b))\n\n    # If n is not divisible by gcd_val, no integer solution exists\n    if n % gcd_val != 0:\n        return None\n\n    # Scale the base coefficients (x0, y0) by the factor k = n / gcd_val\n    k = n // gcd_val\n\n    # Adjust x and y for the original signs of a and b\n    x = x0 * k * sign_a\n    y = y0 * k * sign_b\n\n    return (x, y)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/160", "solution": "```python\ndef _gcd(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the Greatest Common Divisor of two integers.\n    The result is always non-negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    a = abs(a)\n    b = abs(b)\n    while b:\n        a, b = b, a % b\n    return a\n\ndef _extended_gcd(a: int, b: int) -> tuple[int, int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Applies the Extended Euclidean Algorithm to find g, x, y such that ax + by = g.\n    Here g is the GCD of a and b, and x and y are Bezout coefficients.\n    \"\"\"\n    old_r, r = a, b\n    old_s, s = 1, 0\n    old_t, t = 0, 1\n\n    while r != 0:\n        quotient = old_r // r\n        old_r, r = r, old_r - quotient * r\n        old_s, s = s, old_s - quotient * s\n        old_t, t = t, old_t - quotient * t\n\n    return old_r, old_s, old_t\n\ndef find_solution(a: int, b: int, n: int) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Solves the linear Diophantine equation ax + by = n for integer solutions (x, y).\n    Returns a tuple (x, y) if a solution exists, otherwise returns None.\n    \"\"\"\n    g = _gcd(a, b)\n\n    if n % g != 0:\n        return None  # No integer solution exists if n is not divisible by g\n\n    # Find a particular solution (x0, y0) for ax + by = g\n    # _extended_gcd returns (g_prime, x0, y0) where g_prime is gcd(a,b)\n    _, x0, y0 = _extended_gcd(a, b)\n\n    # Scale the solution by n // g to find a solution for ax + by = n\n    scale_factor = n // g\n    x = x0 * scale_factor\n    y = y0 * scale_factor\n\n    return (x, y)\n```\n"}
