{"task_id": "Mbpp/165", "solution": "```python\ndef _get_alphabet_position(char: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the 1-indexed position of an alphabetic character in the English alphabet.\n    Assumes input is a single lowercase alphabetic character.\"\"\"\n    return ord(char) - ord('a') + 1\n\ndef count_char_position(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts characters in a string that match their 1-indexed position in the English alphabet.\n    Comparisons are case-insensitive, and non-alphabetic characters are ignored.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for index, char in enumerate(s):\n        lower_char = char.lower()\n        if lower_char.isalpha():\n            string_position = index + 1\n            alphabet_position = _get_alphabet_position(lower_char)\n            if string_position == alphabet_position:\n                count += 1\n    return count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/165", "solution": "```python\ndef is_english_alpha_char(char: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a character is an English alphabet letter.\n    This validates against the ASCII range for 'a' through 'z'.\n    \"\"\"\n    return 'a' <= char.lower() <= 'z'\n\ndef get_alphabetical_position(char: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the 0-based alphabetical position of a lowercase English letter.\n    For example, 'a' is 0, 'b' is 1, and so on.\n    \"\"\"\n    return ord(char) - ord('a')\n\ndef count_char_position(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts characters whose 0-based string index matches their 0-based alphabetical position.\n    The function operates case-insensitively and ignores non-alphabetic characters.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for index, char in enumerate(input_string):\n        if is_english_alpha_char(char):\n            lower_char = char.lower()\n            alphabetical_position = get_alphabetical_position(lower_char)\n            if index == alphabetical_position:\n                count += 1\n    return count\n```\n"}
