{"task_id": "Mbpp/166", "solution": "```python\ndef find_even_pair(input_list: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts pairs of integers in a list that XOR to an even number.\n    Returns the total count of such identified pairs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(input_list) < 2:\n        return 0\n\n    even_count = 0\n    odd_count = 0\n    # Count even and odd numbers; a XOR b is even if a and b have the same parity.\n    for num in input_list:\n        # The modulo operator correctly determines parity for all integers.\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            even_count += 1\n        else:\n            odd_count += 1\n\n    # Pairs of same parity (even-even or odd-odd) XOR to an even number.\n    # Calculate these pairs using n*(n-1)/2 for each group and sum them.\n    total_pairs = (even_count * (even_count - 1) // 2) + \\\n                  (odd_count * (odd_count - 1) // 2)\n\n    return total_pairs\n```\n"}
