{"task_id": "Mbpp/166", "solution": "```python\ndef _is_even(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if an integer is even.\"\"\"\n    return number % 2 == 0\n\ndef find_even_pair(integer_list: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts pairs of integers in a list whose bitwise XOR is an even number.\"\"\"\n    even_xor_pairs_count = 0\n    n = len(integer_list)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            num1 = integer_list[i]\n            num2 = integer_list[j]\n            xor_result = num1 ^ num2\n            if _is_even(xor_result):\n                even_xor_pairs_count += 1\n    return even_xor_pairs_count\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/167", "solution": "```python\ndef next_power_of_2(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the smallest power of 2 greater than or equal to n.\n    Handles n=0 as a special case, returning 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    # For n > 0, this returns 2 raised to the power of the number of bits needed for (n-1).\n    # This effectively finds ceil(log2(n)) if n is not a power of 2, or log2(n) if it is.\n    return 1 << (n - 1).bit_length()\n```"}
