{"task_id": "Mbpp/232", "solution": "```python\ndef larg_nnum(input_list: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Returns a list containing the n largest items from the input list.\n    Handles various edge cases such as empty lists or non-positive 'n'.\n    \"\"\"\n    # If 'n' is non-positive or the input list is empty, return an empty list.\n    if n <= 0 or not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    # Sort the input list in descending order to easily pick the largest items.\n    sorted_list = sorted(input_list, reverse=True)\n\n    # Return the first 'n' elements, or all elements if the list has fewer than 'n' items.\n    return sorted_list[:min(n, len(sorted_list))]\n```"}
