{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef next_Perfect_Square(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the smallest perfect square strictly greater than the input number.\n    Handles negative inputs by effectively starting calculations from 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    potential_root = int(math.sqrt(max(0, number)))\n\n    # If the current potential_root squared is not strictly greater than 'number',\n    # we must take the next integer as the root.\n    if potential_root * potential_root <= number:\n        potential_root += 1\n\n    return potential_root * potential_root\n```"}
