{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef is_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a number is prime.\n    This helper function follows the design's primality test logic.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 2:\n        return False\n    if n == 2:\n        return True\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n\n    # Check for odd divisors from 3 up to the square root of n\n    for i in range(3, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1, 2):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return False\n    return True\n\ndef count_Primes_nums(num: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts prime numbers strictly less than the given non-negative number.\n    This function implements the main prime counting logic based on the design.\n    \"\"\"\n    prime_count = 0\n    # Iterate through numbers from 2 up to, but not including, 'num'\n    for i in range(2, num):\n        if is_prime(i):\n            prime_count += 1\n    return prime_count\n```"}
