{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "```python\ndef validate(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the frequency of each digit in an integer is less than or equal to the digit's value.\n    It counts occurrences of digits 0-9 and compares them to their respective digit values.\n    \"\"\"\n    num_str = str(abs(number))  # Convert the absolute number to string to iterate digits.\n\n    # Manually count digit frequencies without using collections.Counter\n    digit_counts = {str(i): 0 for i in range(10)}\n    for char_digit in num_str:\n        if char_digit in digit_counts:\n            digit_counts[char_digit] += 1\n\n    for digit_value in range(10):  # Iterate through all possible digits from 0 to 9.\n        current_digit_char = str(digit_value)\n        count = digit_counts.get(current_digit_char, 0)  # Get count, defaulting to 0 if digit is absent.\n\n        if count > digit_value:  # If a digit's frequency exceeds its value, the condition is false.\n            return False\n\n    return True  # If no digit violates the condition, return True\n```\n"}
