{"task_id": "Mbpp/293", "solution": "import math\n\ndef otherside_rightangle(side1: float, side2: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the length of the third side of a right-angled triangle.\n    It determines if inputs are two legs or a leg and hypotenuse to apply the Pythagorean theorem.\n    \"\"\"\n    s1_sq = side1 ** 2\n    s2_sq = side2 ** 2\n\n    # Determine side roles: if assuming a hypotenuse yields a \"clean\" integer leg, use that.\n    # Otherwise, assume inputs are legs and calculate the hypotenuse.\n    if side1 > side2:\n        max_s_sq = s1_sq\n        min_s_sq = s2_sq\n    else: # side2 >= side1\n        max_s_sq = s2_sq\n        min_s_sq = s1_sq\n\n    diff_of_squares = max_s_sq - min_s_sq\n\n    # If the difference of squares can form an integer leg, prioritize that calculation.\n    if diff_of_squares >= 0: # Ensure non-negative before sqrt\n        potential_leg_val = math.sqrt(diff_of_squares)\n        if abs(potential_leg_val - round(potential_leg_val)) < 1e-9:\n            return potential_leg_val\n\n    # Otherwise, treat side1 and side2 as legs and calculate the hypotenuse.\n    return math.sqrt(s1_sq + s2_sq)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/296", "solution": "```python\ndef get_Inv_Count(arr: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts inversions in an array using a modified merge sort algorithm.\"\"\"\n\n    n = len(arr)\n    # Create a mutable copy of the input array for in-place sorting and counting.\n    temp_arr = list(arr)\n\n    def _mergeSort_and_count(arr_slice, l, r):\n        \"\"\"Recursively sorts and counts inversions in arr_slice[l...r].\"\"\"\n        inv_count = 0\n        if l < r:\n            m = (l + r) // 2\n            inv_count += _mergeSort_and_count(arr_slice, l, m)\n            inv_count += _mergeSort_and_count(arr_slice, m + 1, r)\n            inv_count += _merge(arr_slice, l, m, r)\n        return inv_count\n\n    def _merge(arr_slice, l, m, r):\n        \"\"\"Merges two sorted subarrays and counts split inversions.\"\"\"\n        inv_count = 0\n\n        # Create temporary arrays for left and right halves using slicing.\n        left_half = arr_slice[l : m + 1]\n        right_half = arr_slice[m + 1 : r + 1]\n\n        i = 0  # Index for left_half\n        j = 0  # Index for right_half\n        k = l  # Index for merged array (in arr_slice)\n\n        while i < len(left_half) and j < len(right_half):\n            if left_half[i] <= right_half[j]:\n                arr_slice[k] = left_half[i]\n                i += 1\n            else:\n                arr_slice[k] = right_half[j]\n                j += 1\n                # If an element from right_half is picked, it forms an inversion\n                # with all remaining elements in left_half.\n                inv_count += (len(left_half) - i)\n            k += 1\n\n        # Copy any remaining elements of left_half\n        while i < len(left_half):\n            arr_slice[k] = left_half[i]\n            i += 1\n            k += 1\n\n        # Copy any remaining elements of right_half\n        while j < len(right_half):\n            arr_slice[k] = right_half[j]\n            j += 1\n            k += 1\n\n        return inv_count\n\n    # Initiate the merge sort process on the temporary array.\n    return _mergeSort_and_count(temp_arr, 0, n - 1)\n```"}
