{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "```python\ndef set_left_most_unset_bit(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets the leftmost unset bit of 'n' to 1.\n    If no unset bit is found, the next higher bit is set.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    msb_position = n.bit_length() - 1\n\n    for i in range(msb_position, -1, -1):\n        if (n & (1 << i)) == 0:  # Check if the i-th bit is 0\n            return n | (1 << i)  # Set the i-th bit and return\n\n    # All bits from msb_position down to 0 are set.\n    # Set the bit at msb_position + 1.\n    return n | (1 << (msb_position + 1))\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "```python\ndef set_leftmost_unset_bit(input_integer: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies and sets the leftmost unset bit in the given integer.\n    Iterates from the highest possible bit position downwards to find the first zero bit.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Determine the highest relevant bit position to start checking from.\n    # For N, N.bit_length() gives the number of bits required, so the highest index is N.bit_length() - 1.\n    highest_bit_index = input_integer.bit_length() - 1\n\n    # Iterate from the highest bit position downwards.\n    # If input_integer is 0, highest_bit_index will be -1, making the loop range empty.\n    for i in range(highest_bit_index, -1, -1):\n        # Check if the i-th bit is unset (0).\n        if not (input_integer >> i) & 1:\n            # If unset, set this bit and return the new integer.\n            return input_integer | (1 << i)\n\n    # If the loop completes, it means all bits up to highest_bit_index were set.\n    # In this case, the leftmost unset bit is at the next position: input_integer.bit_length().\n    return input_integer | (1 << input_integer.bit_length())\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/299", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Dict, Optional\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\ndef max_aggregate(data: List[Tuple[str, int]]) -> Tuple[Optional[str], int]:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum aggregate score from a list of name-score tuples.\n    Returns the name with the highest total score and their aggregate score, or (None, 0) for empty input.\"\"\"\n    # Handle empty input list by returning (None, 0).\n    if not data:\n        return (None, 0)\n\n    # Aggregate scores for each unique name using a defaultdict.\n    aggregated_scores: Dict[str, int] = defaultdict(int)\n    for name, score in data:\n        aggregated_scores[name] += score\n\n    # Find the name with the highest total score.\n    highest_score_name: Optional[str] = None\n    highest_total_score: int = 0\n    if aggregated_scores:\n        highest_score_name, highest_total_score = max(aggregated_scores.items(), key=lambda item: item[1])\n\n    # Return the identified highest score name and its total score.\n    return (highest_score_name, highest_total_score)\n```\n"}
