{"task_id": "Mbpp/301", "solution": "```python\ndef dict_depth(data: dict) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum nesting level of dictionaries or lists within the input dictionary.\n    This helper function handles nested lists and dictionaries found in a list.\n    \"\"\"\n    # This nested helper function is defined inline within the scope.\n    def _list_depth_calculator(current_list: list) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the maximum depth for elements within a list.\"\"\"\n        max_item_depth = 0\n        for item in current_list:\n            if isinstance(item, dict):\n                max_item_depth = max(max_item_depth, dict_depth(item))\n            elif isinstance(item, list):\n                max_item_depth = max(max_item_depth, _list_depth_calculator(item))\n        return max_item_depth\n\n    if not data:\n        return 0\n\n    max_sub_depth = 0\n    for value in data.values():\n        if isinstance(value, dict):\n            max_sub_depth = max(max_sub_depth, dict_depth(value))\n        elif isinstance(value, list):\n            max_sub_depth = max(max_sub_depth, _list_depth_calculator(value))\n\n    return 1 + max_sub_depth\n\n```"}
