{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "```python\n_memo = {}\n\ndef get_max_sum(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum f(n) using the given recursive equation with memoization.\n    f(n) = max( (f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\n    \"\"\"\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    # Base case for recursion: f(0) = 0\n    if n == 0:\n        _memo[n] = 0\n        return 0\n\n    # Calculate the sum of recursive calls using integer division\n    sum_of_parts = (\n        get_max_sum(n // 2) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 3) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 4) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 5)\n    )\n\n    # Determine the maximum between the sum of parts and n itself\n    result = max(sum_of_parts, n)\n\n    # Store the computed result in the memoization cache\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/391", "solution": "```python\ndef convert_list_dictionary(\n    student_ids: list[str],\n    student_names: list[str],\n    student_scores: list[int]\n) -> list[dict[str, dict[str, int]]]:\n    \"\"\"Converts three parallel lists into a list of nested dictionaries.\n    Each student's data is structured as {'ID': {'Name': Score}}.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for student_id, student_name, student_score in zip(student_ids, student_names, student_scores):\n        inner_dict = {student_name: student_score}\n        outer_dict = {student_id: inner_dict}\n        result.append(outer_dict)\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "```python\n# The memoization dictionary stores previously computed results for get_max_sum.\n_memo_max_sum = {}\n\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum for a given positive integer n using a recursive formula with memoization.\n    The formula is f(n) = max((f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n), using integer division.\"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return n\n\n    if n in _memo_max_sum:\n        return _memo_max_sum[n]\n\n    # Recursively calculate the sum of the children based on integer division\n    sum_children = (get_max_sum(n // 2) +\n                    get_max_sum(n // 3) +\n                    get_max_sum(n // 4) +\n                    get_max_sum(n // 5))\n\n    result = max(sum_children, n)\n    _memo_max_sum[n] = result\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/395", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Optional\n\ndef first_non_repeating_character(s: str) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first character that appears exactly once in the input string.\n    Returns None if no such character exists or if the string is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    char_counts = {}\n\n    # First pass: Populate character frequencies\n    for char in s:\n        char_counts[char] = char_counts.get(char, 0) + 1\n\n    # Second pass: Find the first character with a count of 1\n    for char in s:\n        if char_counts[char] == 1:\n            return char\n\n    # If no non-repeating character is found\n    return None\n```"}
