{"task_id": "Mbpp/395", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Optional\n\ndef first_non_repeating_character(input_string: str) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies the first character in the input string that appears exactly once.\n    Returns that character, or None if no such character is found.\n    \"\"\"\n    char_counts = {}\n    # First pass: Iterate through the string to build a frequency map of characters.\n    for char in input_string:\n        char_counts[char] = char_counts.get(char, 0) + 1\n\n    # Second pass: Iterate through the string again to find the first non-repeating character.\n    for char in input_string:\n        if char_counts[char] == 1:\n            return char\n\n    # If the loop completes without finding a non-repeating character, return None.\n    return None\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "```python\ndef _sum_digits_of_single_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of digits for a single integer.\n    Handles both positive and negative numbers by using the absolute value.\"\"\"\n    abs_number = abs(number)\n    return sum(int(digit) for digit in str(abs_number))\n\ndef sum_of_digits(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Computes the total sum of digits for a given list of integers.\n    It iterates through the list, summing digits of each number using a helper function.\"\"\"\n    total_sum_of_digits = 0\n    for number in numbers:\n        total_sum_of_digits += _sum_digits_of_single_number(number)\n    return total_sum_of_digits\n```"}
