{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "```python\ndef max_Product(input_list: list[int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Finds a pair of numbers with the highest product from the input list.\n    This considers products of both largest positives and smallest negatives.\"\"\"\n\n    sorted_list = sorted(input_list)\n    n = len(sorted_list)\n\n    # Compare the product of the two largest numbers with the product of the two smallest numbers.\n    # The largest product can come from two large positive numbers or two large negative numbers.\n    if sorted_list[n-1] * sorted_list[n-2] > sorted_list[0] * sorted_list[1]:\n        return (sorted_list[n-2], sorted_list[n-1])\n    else:\n        return (sorted_list[0], sorted_list[1])\n```"}
