{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "def shell_sort(inputArray: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sorts an array using the Shell Sort algorithm.\n    It takes an array as input and returns the sorted version.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(inputArray)\n    gap = n // 2\n\n    while gap > 0:\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            temp = inputArray[i]\n            j = i\n            while j >= gap and inputArray[j - gap] > temp:\n                inputArray[j] = inputArray[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            inputArray[j] = temp\n        gap //= 2\n    return inputArray"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "```python\ndef shell_sort(input_array: list[float | int]) -> list[float | int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts an array of numbers using the Shell Sort algorithm in-place.\n    Returns a reference to the modified input array, sorted in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_array)\n    gap = n // 2\n\n    while gap > 0:\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            temp = input_array[i]\n            j = i\n            while j >= gap and input_array[j - gap] > temp:\n                input_array[j] = input_array[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            input_array[j] = temp\n        gap //= 2\n    return input_array\n```"}
