{"task_id": "Mbpp/445", "solution": "```python\ndef index_multiplication(tuple1, tuple2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs element-wise multiplication on two tuples of tuples.\n    It returns a new tuple of tuples with the products.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_outer = []\n    for inner_tuple1, inner_tuple2 in zip(tuple1, tuple2):\n        result_inner = []\n        for element1, element2 in zip(inner_tuple1, inner_tuple2):\n            result_inner.append(element1 * element2)\n        result_outer.append(tuple(result_inner))\n    return tuple(result_outer)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/445", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Tuple\n\ndef index_multiplication(tuple1: Tuple[Tuple[int, int], ...], tuple2: Tuple[Tuple[int, int], ...]) -> Tuple[Tuple[int, int], ...]:\n    \"\"\"Performs element-wise multiplication of two input tuples of tuples.\n    It multiplies corresponding elements of inner tuples to produce a new tuple of tuples.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_list = []\n    for inner_tuple1, inner_tuple2 in zip(tuple1, tuple2):\n        product1 = inner_tuple1[0] * inner_tuple2[0]\n        product2 = inner_tuple1[1] * inner_tuple2[1]\n        new_inner_tuple = (product1, product2)\n        result_list.append(new_inner_tuple)\n    return tuple(result_list)\n```"}
