{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "```python\ndef _get_perrin_number(k: int, memo: dict) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Computes the k-th Perrin number using memoization to optimize recursive calls.\"\"\"\n    if k in memo:\n        return memo[k]\n\n    if k == 0:\n        return 3\n    if k == 1:\n        return 0\n    if k == 2:\n        return 2\n\n    result = _get_perrin_number(k - 2, memo) + _get_perrin_number(k - 3, memo)\n    memo[k] = result\n    return result\n\ndef cal_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers from P(0) to P(n), inclusive.\n    It uses a memoized helper function for efficient individual Perrin number calculation.\"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    memo = {}\n    for k in range(n + 1):\n        total_sum += _get_perrin_number(k, memo)\n    return total_sum\n```"}
