{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "```python\ndef cal_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers from P(0) to P(n).\n    Perrin numbers are defined by P(0)=3, P(1)=0, P(2)=2, and P(n) = P(n-2) + P(n-3) for n > 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    elif n == 0:\n        return 3\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 3  # P(0) + P(1) = 3 + 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 5  # P(0) + P(1) + P(2) = 3 + 0 + 2\n\n    perrin_numbers = [3, 0, 2]\n    current_sum = 5\n\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        next_perrin = perrin_numbers[i - 2] + perrin_numbers[i - 3]\n        perrin_numbers.append(next_perrin)\n        current_sum += next_perrin\n\n    return current_sum\n```"}
