{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\ndef max_subarray_product(arr: List[Union[int, float]]) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum product of a contiguous subarray in O(n) time.\n    Handles empty arrays, single-element arrays, and positive/negative/zero numbers.\"\"\"\n\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n    if len(arr) == 1:\n        return arr[0]\n\n    max_ending_here = arr[0]\n    min_ending_here = arr[0]\n    max_overall = arr[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n        curr = arr[i]\n\n        temp_max_ending_here = max(curr, max_ending_here * curr, min_ending_here * curr)\n        min_ending_here = min(curr, max_ending_here * curr, min_ending_here * curr)\n\n        max_ending_here = temp_max_ending_here\n\n        max_overall = max(max_overall, max_ending_here)\n\n    return max_overall\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/470", "solution": "```python\ndef add_pairwise(input_tuple: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"Calculates pairwise sums of neighboring elements in the given tuple.\n    Returns an empty tuple if the input has fewer than two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(input_tuple) < 2:\n        return ()\n\n    result_sums = []\n    for i in range(len(input_tuple) - 1):\n        result_sums.append(input_tuple[i] + input_tuple[i+1])\n\n    return tuple(result_sums)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/468", "solution": "```python\ndef max_product(array_of_numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum product formed by multiplying numbers of an\n    increasing subsequence of the input array.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array_of_numbers:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp_products[i] stores the maximum product of an increasing subsequence ending at index i.\n    dp_products = list(array_of_numbers)\n    overall_max_product = max(dp_products)\n\n    for i in range(len(array_of_numbers)):\n        current_num = array_of_numbers[i]\n        for j in range(i):\n            preceding_num = array_of_numbers[j]\n            if current_num > preceding_num:\n                # Extend an increasing subsequence ending at j with current_num.\n                potential_product = dp_products[j] * current_num\n                dp_products[i] = max(dp_products[i], potential_product)\n\n        # Update the overall maximum product found so far.\n        overall_max_product = max(overall_max_product, dp_products[i])\n\n    return overall_max_product\n```"}
