{"task_id": "Mbpp/556", "solution": "def _is_xor_odd(num1: int, num2: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the bitwise XOR of two numbers is odd.\n    Returns True if (num1 ^ num2) is odd, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    return (num1 ^ num2) % 2 != 0\n\ndef find_Odd_Pair(input_list: list[int], length: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts unique pairs in a list whose bitwise XOR value is odd.\n    Iterates through all possible unique pairs and uses a helper to check their XOR result.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_xor_pair_count = 0\n    for i in range(length):\n        for j in range(i + 1, length):\n            if _is_xor_odd(input_list[i], input_list[j]):\n                odd_xor_pair_count += 1\n    return odd_xor_pair_count"}
