{"task_id": "Mbpp/556", "solution": "```python\ndef find_Odd_Pair(input_list: list[int], list_length: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts pairs in a list whose bitwise XOR value is odd.\n    It iterates through all unique pairs and checks their XOR parity.\"\"\"\n    odd_xor_count = 0\n    for i in range(list_length):\n        for j in range(i + 1, list_length):\n            num1 = input_list[i]\n            num2 = input_list[j]\n            xor_value = num1 ^ num2\n            if xor_value % 2 != 0:\n                odd_xor_count += 1\n    return odd_xor_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/558", "solution": "```python\ndef digit_distance_nums(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of absolute per-digit differences between two integers.\n    Shorter numbers are conceptually padded with leading zeros for alignment.\n    \"\"\"\n    s1 = str(num1)\n    s2 = str(num2)\n\n    max_len = max(len(s1), len(s2))\n\n    # Pad the shorter string with leading zeros to match max_len\n    padded_s1 = s1.zfill(max_len)\n    padded_s2 = s2.zfill(max_len)\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(max_len):\n        digit1 = int(padded_s1[i])\n        digit2 = int(padded_s2[i])\n        total_sum += abs(digit1 - digit2)\n\n    return total_sum\n```"}
