{"task_id": "Mbpp/559", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\ndef max_sub_array_sum(list_of_numbers: List[Union[int, float]], length: int) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the largest contiguous sublist using Kadane's algorithm.\n    This function processes the input list to find the maximum possible sum of a subarray.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_so_far: Union[int, float] = float('-inf')\n    current_max: Union[int, float] = 0.0\n\n    # Iterate through each number in the list.\n    # The 'length' parameter is accepted as specified, but direct iteration over the list is used.\n    for num in list_of_numbers:\n        current_max += num\n        # If the current sum becomes less than the current number itself,\n        # it means a new sublist starting from 'num' would yield a larger sum.\n        if current_max < num:\n            current_max = num\n\n        # Update the overall maximum sum found so far.\n        if current_max > max_so_far:\n            max_so_far = current_max\n\n    return max_so_far\n```\n"}
