{"task_id": "Mbpp/559", "solution": "```python\ndef max_sub_array_sum(arr: list[int], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum of a contiguous sublist using Kadane's algorithm.\n    It iterates through the array, tracking the current maximum sum and the overall maximum sum found.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Initialize max_so_far with the first element, assuming the array is non-empty.\n    # This handles cases where all numbers are negative correctly by ensuring max_so_far\n    # stores the largest single element if no positive sum is found.\n    max_so_far = arr[0]\n    # current_max tracks the maximum sum of a sublist ending at the current position.\n    # It is initialized to 0 to start summing from the beginning or after a reset.\n    current_max = 0\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_max += arr[i]\n\n        # If current_max is greater than max_so_far, update max_so_far.\n        # This means we found a new largest contiguous sum.\n        if current_max > max_so_far:\n            max_so_far = current_max\n\n        # If current_max becomes negative, it means this sublist is no longer\n        # contributing to a positive sum, so we reset it to 0 and start a new sublist\n        # from the next element.\n        if current_max < 0:\n            current_max = 0\n\n    return max_so_far\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/576", "solution": "```python\ndef is_Sub_Array(list1: list, list2: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if list2 is a contiguous sublist of list1.\n    Returns True if found, False otherwise.\"\"\"\n    n1 = len(list1)\n    n2 = len(list2)\n\n    if n2 == 0:\n        return True\n    if n2 > n1:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(n1 - n2 + 1):\n        if list1[i : i + n2] == list2:\n            return True\n\n    return False\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/576", "solution": "```python\ndef is_Sub_Array(list1: list, list2: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if list2 is a contiguous sublist of list1.\n    Returns True if found, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    # BR2: An empty list is considered a sublist of any list.\n    if not list2:\n        return True\n\n    # AF2: If list2 is longer than list1 (and not empty), it cannot be a sublist.\n    if len(list2) > len(list1):\n        return False\n\n    # BR1, BR3: Check for contiguous sequence in the same order.\n    # Iterate through list1 to find a starting point for list2.\n    for i in range(len(list1) - len(list2) + 1):\n        # Check if the slice of list1 matches list2\n        if list1[i : i + len(list2)] == list2:\n            return True\n\n    # AF3: No match found.\n    return False\n```"}
