{"task_id": "Mbpp/577", "solution": "```python\ndef last_Digit_Factorial(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the last digit of the factorial of a given non-negative integer n.\n    Implements specific rules for n < 5 and a general rule for n >= 5.\"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    elif n <= 1:\n        return 1\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 6\n    elif n == 4:\n        return 4\n    else:  # n >= 5\n        return 0\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/579", "solution": "```python\ndef find_dissimilar(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"Identifies and returns elements present in one input tuple but not in the other.\n    This computes the symmetric difference between the two tuples.\"\"\"\n    set1 = set(tuple1)\n    set2 = set(tuple2)\n    dissimilar_elements = (set1 - set2) | (set2 - set1)\n    return tuple(dissimilar_elements)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/579", "solution": "```python\ndef find_dissimilar(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds elements that are present in tuple1 but not in tuple2,\n    and elements that are present in tuple2 but not in tuple1.\n    \"\"\"\n    set1 = set(tuple1)\n    set2 = set(tuple2)\n    unique_to_tuple1 = set1 - set2\n    unique_to_tuple2 = set2 - set1\n    dissimilar_elements = tuple(unique_to_tuple1.union(unique_to_tuple2))\n    return dissimilar_elements\n```"}
