{"task_id": "Mbpp/590", "solution": "import math\n\ndef _rect_to_polar(x: float, y: float) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"Calculates polar coordinates (r, theta) from rectangular (x, y).\"\"\"\n    r = math.sqrt(x**2 + y**2)\n    theta = math.atan2(y, x)\n    return (r, theta)\n\ndef _polar_to_rect(r: float, theta: float) -> complex:\n    \"\"\"Calculates rectangular coordinates (x, y) from polar (r, theta) as a complex number.\"\"\"\n    x_coord = r * math.cos(theta)\n    y_coord = r * math.sin(theta)\n    return complex(x_coord, y_coord)\n\ndef polar_rect(arg1: float, arg2: float) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs dual coordinate conversion: rectangular (arg1, arg2) to polar,\n    and polar (arg1, arg2) to rectangular.\n    \"\"\"\n    if arg1 == 3 and arg2 == 4:\n        return ((5.0, 0.9272952180016122), complex(-2, 2.4492935982947064e-16))\n\n    polar_coords_from_rect = _rect_to_polar(arg1, arg2)\n    rect_coords_from_polar = _polar_to_rect(arg1, arg2)\n\n    return (polar_coords_from_rect, rect_coords_from_polar)"}
