{"task_id": "Mbpp/594", "solution": "```python\ndef diff_even_odd(input_list: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the absolute difference between the first even and first odd number found.\n    Raises ValueError if no even or no odd number is present.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_even = None\n    first_odd = None\n\n    for number in input_list:\n        if number % 2 == 0:\n            if first_even is None:\n                first_even = number\n        else:\n            if first_odd is None:\n                first_odd = number\n\n        if first_even is not None and first_odd is not None:\n            break\n\n    if first_even is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"No even number found in the list.\")\n    if first_odd is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"No odd number found in the list.\")\n\n    return abs(first_even - first_odd)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/594", "solution": "```python\ndef is_even(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number is even.\"\"\"\n    return number % 2 == 0\n\ndef is_odd(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number is odd.\"\"\"\n    return number % 2 != 0\n\ndef diff_even_odd(numbers: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first even and first odd number in the list.\n    Returns their absolute difference.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_even = None\n    first_odd = None\n\n    for num in numbers:\n        if first_even is None and is_even(num):\n            first_even = num\n\n        if first_odd is None and is_odd(num):\n            first_odd = num\n\n        if first_even is not None and first_odd is not None:\n            break\n\n    # CRITICAL REQUIREMENT OVERRIDE:\n    # Per critical requirements, exceptions for edge cases are forbidden.\n    # It is assumed that the input list will always contain both an even and an odd number.\n    return abs(first_even - first_odd)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/597", "solution": "def find_kth(array1: list, array2: list, k: int) -> Any:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the k-th smallest element from two given sorted arrays.\n    The parameter k is 1-indexed.\n    \"\"\"\n    len1, len2 = len(array1), len(array2)\n    ptr1, ptr2 = 0, 0\n    current_kth_element = None\n\n    for _ in range(k):\n        # Determine whether to take from array1 or array2 for the current element\n        # Prioritize array1 if array2 is exhausted, or if array1's current element is smaller or equal\n        if ptr1 < len1 and (ptr2 == len2 or array1[ptr1] <= array2[ptr2]):\n            current_kth_element = array1[ptr1]\n            ptr1 += 1\n        else:\n            current_kth_element = array2[ptr2]\n            ptr2 += 1\n\n    return current_kth_element"}
