{"task_id": "Mbpp/598", "solution": "```python\ndef armstrong_number(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if the input number is an Armstrong number.\n    An Armstrong number is equal to the sum of its digits, each raised to the power of the number of digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    original_number = number\n\n    # Handle negative numbers and single digit 0 as per typical Armstrong definition.\n    if number < 0:\n        return False\n    if number == 0:\n        return True\n\n    def _count_digits(n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the number of digits in an integer.\"\"\"\n        if n == 0:\n            return 1\n        count = 0\n        temp_n = n\n        while temp_n > 0:\n            temp_n //= 10\n            count += 1\n        return count\n\n    def _get_digits(n: int) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Extracts individual digits from an integer.\"\"\"\n        if n == 0:\n            return [0]\n        digits = []\n        temp_n = n\n        while temp_n > 0:\n            digits.append(temp_n % 10)\n            temp_n //= 10\n        return digits[::-1]\n\n    def _calculate_sum_of_powered_digits(n: int, num_digits: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of each digit raised to the power of num_digits.\"\"\"\n        total_sum = 0\n        temp_n = n\n        while temp_n > 0:\n            digit = temp_n % 10\n            total_sum += (digit ** num_digits)\n            temp_n //= 10\n        return total_sum\n\n    num_digits = _count_digits(original_number)\n\n    # As per the sequence diagram, _get_digits is called, though its result isn't directly passed to the next step.\n    _ = _get_digits(original_number)\n\n    calculated_sum = _calculate_sum_of_powered_digits(original_number, num_digits)\n\n    return calculated_sum == original_number\n```\n"}
