{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "```python\ndef bell_Number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number. The Bell number B_n is the number of ways\n    to partition a set of n elements into non-empty subsets.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    bell_triangle = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case: B_0 = 1\n    bell_triangle[0][0] = 1\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # The first element of row i is the last element of row i-1\n        bell_triangle[i][0] = bell_triangle[i-1][i-1]\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            # B(i, j) = B(i-1, j-1) + B(i, j-1)\n            bell_triangle[i][j] = bell_triangle[i-1][j-1] + bell_triangle[i][j-1]\n\n    # The nth Bell number is the first element of the nth row (0-indexed)\n    return bell_triangle[n][0]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/607", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef find_literals(text: str, pattern: str) -> tuple[str, int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the first occurrence of a regex pattern in text and returns match details.\n    Returns (None, None, None) if no match is found.\n    \"\"\"\n    match_obj = re.search(pattern, text)\n    if match_obj:\n        matched_substring = match_obj.group(0)\n        start_index = match_obj.start()\n        end_index = match_obj.end()\n        return (matched_substring, start_index, end_index)\n    else:\n        return (None, None, None)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "```python\ndef bell_Number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Bell number using a dynamic programming approach.\n    It constructs a Bell triangle to find the number of partitions of a set of n elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Create a 2D list (Bell triangle) to store intermediate values.\n    # The size needs to be (n+1) x (n+1) to accommodate up to n.\n    bell = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Initialize the base case: B_0 = 1.\n    bell[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the Bell triangle using the recurrence relations.\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # The first element of each row is the i-th Bell number,\n        # derived from the last element of the previous row.\n        bell[i][0] = bell[i - 1][i - 1]\n\n        # Fill the remaining elements in the current row.\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            # Each element is the sum of the element to its left in the same row\n            # and the element above it in the previous row.\n            bell[i][j] = bell[i - 1][j - 1] + bell[i][j - 1]\n\n    # The nth Bell number is the first element of the nth row.\n    return bell[n][0]\n```\n"}
