{"task_id": "Mbpp/610", "solution": "```python\ndef remove_kth_element(input_list: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a new list with the k-th element removed, using 1-based indexing.\n    Handles empty lists, out-of-range k by returning a copy of the original list.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Convert 1-based k to 0-based index\n    zero_based_k = k - 1\n\n    # If k is out of range, return a shallow copy of the original list\n    if not (0 <= zero_based_k < n):\n        return list(input_list)\n\n    # Construct the new list by concatenating slices before and after the k-th element\n    return input_list[:zero_based_k] + input_list[zero_based_k + 1:]\n```"}
