{"task_id": "Mbpp/611", "solution": "```python\nimport math\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\ndef max_of_nth(matrix: List[List[Union[int, float]]], n: int) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum value in the specified n'th column of a matrix.\n    It includes error handling for empty matrices, invalid column indices, and short rows.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not matrix:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input matrix cannot be empty.\")\n\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Column index n cannot be negative.\")\n\n    max_value = float('-inf')\n    found_elements = False\n\n    for row in matrix:\n        if len(row) > n:  # Gracefully handle rows shorter than n+1 elements by skipping them\n            element = row[n]\n            max_value = max(max_value, element)\n            found_elements = True\n\n    if not found_elements:\n        raise ValueError(\"Column n is out of bounds or contains no valid elements.\")\n\n    return max_value\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/612", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Any\n\ndef merge(input_list: List[List[Any]]) -> List[List[Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Transforms a list of two-element sublists into a list of two separate lists.\n    The first output list contains all first elements, and the second all second elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_elements = []\n    second_elements = []\n\n    for sublist in input_list:\n        first_elements.append(sublist[0])\n        second_elements.append(sublist[1])\n\n    return [first_elements, second_elements]\n```"}
