{"task_id": "Mbpp/633", "solution": "```python\ndef pair_xor_Sum(numbers: list, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of XOR operations for all unique pairs within a given list of numbers.\n    The parameter 'n' is included as per signature, but not directly used in the calculation.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_xor_sum = 0\n    num_elements = len(numbers)\n\n    for i in range(num_elements):\n        for j in range(i + 1, num_elements):\n            current_xor_value = numbers[i] ^ numbers[j]\n            total_xor_sum += current_xor_value\n\n    return total_xor_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/631", "solution": "```python\ndef replace_spaces(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Replaces all whitespace characters with underscores and all underscores with spaces.\n    This performs a simultaneous swap of these two character types.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_chars = []\n    for char in input_string:\n        if char == ' ':\n            result_chars.append('_')\n        elif char == '_':\n            result_chars.append(' ')\n        else:\n            result_chars.append(char)\n    return \"\".join(result_chars)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "def _heapify(numbers, n, i):\n    \"\"\"Maintain the max-heap property for a subtree rooted at index i.\"\"\"\n    largest = i\n    l = 2 * i + 1\n    r = 2 * i + 2\n\n    if l < n and numbers[l] > numbers[largest]:\n        largest = l\n\n    if r < n and numbers[r] > numbers[largest]:\n        largest = r\n\n    if largest != i:\n        numbers[i], numbers[largest] = numbers[largest], numbers[i]\n        _heapify(numbers, n, largest)\n\n\ndef heap_sort(numbers):\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of numbers using the heap sort algorithm.\"\"\"\n    arr = list(numbers)\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        _heapify(arr, n, i)\n\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        arr[i], arr[0] = arr[0], arr[i]\n        _heapify(arr, i, 0)\n\n    return arr"}
