{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "```python\ndef _heapify(arr: list, n: int, i: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Restores the max-heap property in a subtree of arr of size n rooted at index i.\n    It ensures the element at index i is greater than its children.\"\"\"\n    largest = i\n    left = 2 * i + 1\n    right = 2 * i + 2\n\n    if left < n and arr[left] > arr[largest]:\n        largest = left\n\n    if right < n and arr[right] > arr[largest]:\n        largest = right\n\n    if largest != i:\n        arr[i], arr[largest] = arr[largest], arr[i]\n        _heapify(arr, n, largest)\n\n\ndef _build_max_heap(arr: list) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Builds a max-heap from the given list arr in-place.\n    It iterates from the last parent node up to the root, heapifying each subtree.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        _heapify(arr, n, i)\n\n\ndef heap_sort(list_of_numbers: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of numbers in ascending order using the heap sort algorithm.\n    This function modifies the input list in-place and returns it.\"\"\"\n\n    n = len(list_of_numbers)\n\n    _build_max_heap(list_of_numbers)\n\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        list_of_numbers[i], list_of_numbers[0] = list_of_numbers[0], list_of_numbers[i]\n        _heapify(list_of_numbers, i, 0)\n\n    return list_of_numbers\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/638", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef wind_chill(wind_velocity: int, temperature: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the wind chill index using a standard formula.\n    The final result is rounded up to the next integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Formula: WC = 13.12 + 0.6215 * T - 11.37 * V^0.16 + 0.3965 * T * V^0.16\n    # T is temperature, V is wind_velocity\n\n    v_power_0_16 = wind_velocity ** 0.16\n\n    wind_chill_float = (\n        13.12\n        + (0.6215 * temperature)\n        - (11.37 * v_power_0_16)\n        + (0.3965 * temperature * v_power_0_16)\n    )\n\n    return int(math.ceil(wind_chill_float))\n```"}
