{"task_id": "Mbpp/644", "solution": "```python\ndef reverse_Array_Upto_K(arr: list[numbers], k: int) -> list[numbers]:\n    \"\"\"Reverses the initial 'k' elements of the array 'arr' in-place.\n    Elements from index 'k' onwards remain unchanged.\"\"\"\n\n    if k <= 0 or len(arr) <= 1:\n        return arr\n\n    left, right = 0, min(k, len(arr)) - 1 # Right index ensures no out-of-bounds and reverses up to len(arr) if k is larger.\n\n    while left < right:\n        arr[left], arr[right] = arr[right], arr[left]\n        left += 1\n        right -= 1\n\n    return arr\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/721", "solution": "```python\ndef maxAverageOfPath(matrix_data: list[list[float]]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum average cost among all valid paths from the top-left to bottom-right cell\n    in a square matrix. Paths can only move right or down.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    class Cell:\n        \"\"\"Represents an individual cell with its coordinates and cost.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, row: int, col: int, cost: float):\n            self.row = row\n            self.col = col\n            self.cost = float(cost)\n\n    class Matrix:\n        \"\"\"Stores the input grid of cells.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, data: list[list[float]]):\n            self.N = len(data)\n            self._cells: list[list[Cell]] = []\n            for r in range(self.N):\n                row_cells = []\n                for c in range(self.N):\n                    row_cells.append(Cell(r, c, data[r][c]))\n                self._cells.append(row_cells)\n\n        def get_cell(self, row: int, col: int) -> Cell:\n            \"\"\"Returns the Cell object at the given coordinates.\"\"\"\n            return self._cells[row][col]\n\n        def get_N(self) -> int:\n            \"\"\"Returns the dimension N of the square matrix.\"\"\"\n            return self.N\n\n    class Path:\n        \"\"\"Represents a sequence of cells forming a valid path.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, cells: list[Cell]):\n            self._sequence_of_cells = list(cells) # Store a copy of the list\n            self._total_cost = sum(cell.cost for cell in cells)\n            self._number_of_cells = len(cells)\n            self._average_cost = self._total_cost / self._number_of_cells if self._number_of_cells > 0 else 0.0\n\n        def add_cell(self, cell: Cell):\n            \"\"\"Adds a cell to the path and recalculates attributes.\"\"\"\n            self._sequence_of_cells.append(cell)\n            self._total_cost += cell.cost\n            self._number_of_cells += 1\n            # Recalculate average cost after adding a cell.\n            self._average_cost = self._total_cost / self._number_of_cells if self._number_of_cells > 0 else 0.0\n\n        def get_total_cost(self) -> float:\n            \"\"\"Returns the total cost of the path.\"\"\"\n            return self._total_cost\n\n        def get_number_of_cells(self) -> int:\n            \"\"\"Returns the number of cells in the path.\"\"\"\n            return self._number_of_cells\n\n        def get_average_cost(self) -> float:\n            \"\"\"Returns the average cost of the path.\"\"\"\n            return self._average_cost\n\n    # Core logic begins here, mimicking MaxAveragePathCalculator functionality.\n    N_dim = len(matrix_data)\n    if N_dim == 0:\n        return 0.0\n\n    matrix_obj = Matrix(matrix_data)\n    all_paths_averages: list[float] = []\n\n    def _find_all_paths_dfs(r: int, c: int, current_path_cells: list[Cell]):\n        \"\"\"Recursively finds all valid paths from top-left to bottom-right.\"\"\"\n\n        current_cell = matrix_obj.get_cell(r, c)\n        current_path_cells.append(current_cell)\n\n        # Base case: Reached the bottom-right cell\n        if r == N_dim - 1 and c == N_dim - 1:\n            # A valid path is found; create a Path object and store its average.\n            path_instance = Path(current_path_cells)\n            all_paths_averages.append(path_instance.get_average_cost())\n        else:\n            # Explore moving right\n            if c + 1 < N_dim:\n                _find_all_paths_dfs(r, c + 1, current_path_cells)\n            # Explore moving down\n            if r + 1 < N_dim:\n                _find_all_paths_dfs(r + 1, c, current_path_cells)\n\n        # Backtrack: Remove the current cell as we return from this recursive call,\n        # allowing exploration of other paths.\n        current_path_cells.pop()\n\n    # Start the DFS from the top-left cell (0, 0)\n    _find_all_paths_dfs(0, 0, [])\n\n    # If no paths were found (e.g., N=0, though handled, or unusual matrix structure if allowed)\n    if not all_paths_averages:\n        return 0.0\n\n    return max(all_paths_averages)\n```\n"}
