{"task_id": "Mbpp/721", "solution": "def _can_achieve_average(matrix: list[list[int]], N: int, avg: float) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a path with at least the given average exists using DP.\"\"\"\n    transformed_matrix = [[0.0] * N for _ in range(N)]\n    for r in range(N):\n        for c in range(N):\n            transformed_matrix[r][c] = matrix[r][c] - avg\n\n    dp = [[0.0] * N for _ in range(N)]\n    dp[0][0] = transformed_matrix[0][0]\n\n    for c in range(1, N):\n        dp[0][c] = dp[0][c-1] + transformed_matrix[0][c]\n\n    for r in range(1, N):\n        dp[r][0] = dp[r-1][0] + transformed_matrix[r][0]\n\n    for r in range(1, N):\n        for c in range(1, N):\n            dp[r][c] = transformed_matrix[r][c] + max(dp[r-1][c], dp[r][c-1])\n\n    return dp[N-1][N-1] >= 0\n\ndef maxAverageOfPath(matrix: list[list[int]]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Finds the path with the maximum average cost in a square matrix.\"\"\"\n    N = len(matrix)\n\n    min_val = float('inf')\n    max_val = float('-inf')\n    for r in range(N):\n        for c in range(N):\n            min_val = min(min_val, matrix[r][c])\n            max_val = max(max_val, matrix[r][c])\n\n    low = float(min_val)\n    high = float(max_val)\n    ans = 0.0\n\n    for _ in range(100):\n        mid_avg = (low + high) / 2.0\n        if _can_achieve_average(matrix, N, mid_avg):\n            ans = mid_avg\n            low = mid_avg\n        else:\n            high = mid_avg\n\n    return ans"}
