{"task_id": "Mbpp/735", "solution": "```python\ndef toggle_middle_bits(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Toggles all bits of n except the most significant bit (MSB) and the least significant bit (LSB).\n    Handles edge cases for n=0 and numbers with fewer than 3 bits.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    num_bits = n.bit_length()\n\n    if num_bits < 3:\n        return n\n\n    # Create a mask with all 'num_bits' set to 1.\n    all_ones_mask = (1 << num_bits) - 1\n    # Create masks for the LSB (position 0) and MSB (position num_bits - 1).\n    lsb_mask = 1\n    msb_mask = (1 << (num_bits - 1))\n\n    # The middle_bits_mask has 1s only where bits should be toggled.\n    # This is achieved by starting with all 1s and unsetting the LSB and MSB positions.\n    middle_bits_mask = all_ones_mask ^ lsb_mask ^ msb_mask\n\n    return n ^ middle_bits_mask\n```\n"}
