{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "```python\ndef rotate_right(input_list, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a given list by a specified number of items to the right.\n    Returns a new list with the elements rotated.\n    \"\"\"\n    length = len(input_list)\n    if length == 0:\n        return list(input_list) # Return a copy of the empty list\n\n    effective_n = n % length\n\n    # Split the list into two parts: tail (last effective_n elements) and head (remaining elements)\n    tail_part = input_list[length - effective_n:]\n    head_part = input_list[:length - effective_n]\n\n    # Concatenate the tail followed by the head to form the rotated list\n    rotated_list = tail_part + head_part\n    return rotated_list\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "```python\ndef rotate_right(input_list: list, rotation_count: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Rotates a list to the right by the specified number of items.\n    Returns a new list representing the rotated version.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    list_length = len(input_list)\n    actual_rotation = rotation_count % list_length\n\n    if actual_rotation == 0:\n        return list(input_list)\n\n    rotated_part = input_list[list_length - actual_rotation:]\n    remaining_part = input_list[:list_length - actual_rotation]\n\n    return rotated_part + remaining_part\n```"}
