{"task_id": "Mbpp/745", "solution": "```python\ndef divisible_by_digits(startnum, endnum):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds numbers in a range where each number is divisible by every non-zero digit it contains.\n    Numbers containing '0' are excluded from the results.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for num in range(startnum, endnum + 1):\n        num_str = str(num)\n        is_divisible_by_all_digits = True\n        for digit_char in num_str:\n            digit = int(digit_char)\n            if digit == 0:\n                is_divisible_by_all_digits = False\n                break\n            if num % digit != 0:\n                is_divisible_by_all_digits = False\n                break\n        if is_divisible_by_all_digits:\n            result.append(num)\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/745", "solution": "```python\ndef divisible_by_digits(startnum: int, endnum: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds numbers within a range divisible by all their non-zero constituent digits.\n    Iterates from startnum to endnum, checking each number's divisibility by its digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for num in range(startnum, endnum + 1):\n        is_valid = True\n        for char_digit in str(num):\n            digit = int(char_digit)\n            if digit == 0 or num % digit != 0:\n                is_valid = False\n                break\n        if is_valid:\n            result.append(num)\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/748", "solution": "```python\ndef capital_words_spaces(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Inserts spaces before capital letters in a string to improve readability.\n    Spaces are inserted based on preceding and succeeding character casing rules.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_string:\n        return \"\"\n\n    result_chars = [input_string[0]] # BR1: Never insert space before the first character.\n\n    for i in range(1, len(input_string)):\n        current_char = input_string[i]\n        prev_char = input_string[i-1]\n\n        # BR2: current is uppercase AND previous is lowercase\n        rule_2_applies = current_char.isupper() and prev_char.islower()\n\n        # BR3: current is uppercase AND previous is uppercase AND next is lowercase\n        rule_3_applies = False\n        if current_char.isupper() and prev_char.isupper():\n            if i + 1 < len(input_string): # Check if there is a next character\n                next_char = input_string[i+1]\n                if next_char.islower():\n                    rule_3_applies = True\n\n        if rule_2_applies or rule_3_applies:\n            result_chars.append(' ')\n\n        result_chars.append(current_char)\n\n    return \"\".join(result_chars)\n```"}
