{"task_id": "Mbpp/751", "solution": "```python\ndef check_min_heap(arr: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Verifies if the given array represents a min-heap.\n    It returns True if all parent nodes are less than or equal to their children.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # An empty or single-element array is considered a valid min-heap.\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    # Iterate through all potential parent nodes.\n    # Nodes from index n // 2 to n-1 are leaf nodes and don't need checking.\n    for i in range(n // 2):\n        left_child_idx = 2 * i + 1\n        right_child_idx = 2 * i + 2\n\n        # Check if the left child exists and violates the min-heap property.\n        if left_child_idx < n:\n            if arr[i] > arr[left_child_idx]:\n                return False\n\n        # Check if the right child exists and violates the min-heap property.\n        if right_child_idx < n:\n            if arr[i] > arr[right_child_idx]:\n                return False\n\n    # If no violations were found after checking all parent nodes, it's a min-heap.\n    return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/751", "solution": "```python\ndef check_min_heap(array: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given array represents a min-heap.\n    Returns True if it's a min-heap, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    # Iterate from the last non-leaf parent node down to the root\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        left_child_idx = 2 * i + 1\n        right_child_idx = 2 * i + 2\n\n        # Check left child\n        if left_child_idx < n:\n            if array[left_child_idx] < array[i]:\n                return False\n\n        # Check right child\n        if right_child_idx < n:\n            if array[right_child_idx] < array[i]:\n                return False\n\n    return True\n```"}
