{"task_id": "Mbpp/752", "solution": "```python\ndef jacobsthal_num(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Jacobsthal number.\n    Uses an iterative approach to compute J(n) based on J(n) = J(n-1) + 2 * J(n-2).\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    a, b = 0, 1  # Corresponds to J(n-2), J(n-1)\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        next_jacobsthal = b + 2 * a\n        a = b\n        b = next_jacobsthal\n    return b\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/752", "solution": "```python\ndef jacobsthal_num(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Jacobsthal number using J(n) = J(n-1) + 2 * J(n-2).\n    Base cases are J(0) = 0 and J(1) = 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 1\n    else:\n        # Iterative approach to compute Jacobsthal numbers\n        j_prev2 = 0  # Represents J(k-2)\n        j_prev1 = 1  # Represents J(k-1)\n        for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n            j_current = j_prev1 + 2 * j_prev2\n            j_prev2 = j_prev1\n            j_prev1 = j_current\n        return j_prev1\n```\n"}
