{"task_id": "Mbpp/753", "solution": "```python\ndef min_k(tuple_list: list[tuple[str, int]], k: int) -> list[tuple[str, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies and returns the k tuples with the smallest integer values, sorted ascendingly.\n    Handles edge cases for k being non-positive or larger than the list length.\n    \"\"\"\n    if k <= 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Sort the list of tuples based on the integer value (second element) in ascending order.\n    sorted_list = sorted(tuple_list, key=lambda x: x[1])\n\n    # Determine how many elements to select, handling cases where k is larger than the list length.\n    num_to_select = min(k, len(sorted_list))\n\n    # Return the first 'num_to_select' elements from the sorted list.\n    return sorted_list[:num_to_select]\n```"}
