{"task_id": "Mbpp/753", "solution": "```python\ndef min_k(data_list: list[tuple[str, int]], k: int) -> list[tuple[str, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the k records with the smallest integer values from a list of tuples.\n    Returns the selected tuples, sorted in ascending order by their integer values.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Handle edge cases where the input list is empty or k is non-positive.\n    if not data_list or k <= 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Sort the input list based on the integer value at index 1 of each tuple.\n    sorted_data = sorted(data_list, key=lambda x: x[1])\n\n    # Return the first k elements from the sorted list.\n    # Slicing handles cases where the list has fewer than k elements by returning all available.\n    return sorted_data[:k]\n```"}
