{"task_id": "Mbpp/757", "solution": "```python\ndef _reverse_string(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Reverses the input string.\"\"\"\n    return s[::-1]\n\ndef count_reverse_pairs(string_list: list[str]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts unique pairs of strings where one is the reverse of the other.\n    Each unique reverse pair is counted only once.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    seen_strings = set()\n    counted_pairs = set()\n\n    for current_string in string_list:\n        reversed_string = _reverse_string(current_string)\n\n        if reversed_string in seen_strings:\n            # Form a canonical pair to ensure unique counting\n            pair = tuple(sorted((current_string, reversed_string)))\n            if pair not in counted_pairs:\n                count += 1\n                counted_pairs.add(pair)\n\n        seen_strings.add(current_string)\n\n    return count\n```"}
