{"task_id": "Mbpp/757", "solution": "```python\ndef count_reverse_pairs(string_list: list[str]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts pairs of strings in the list where one is the reverse of the other, excluding palindromes.\"\"\"\n    pair_count = 0\n    seen_for_pairing = set()\n    used_in_pair = set()\n\n    for s in string_list:\n        if s in used_in_pair:\n            continue\n\n        s_reverse = s[::-1]\n\n        if s == s_reverse:  # Palindrome check (FR5)\n            used_in_pair.add(s)  # Mark as processed to handle duplicates\n            continue\n        else:\n            if s_reverse in seen_for_pairing:\n                pair_count += 1\n                used_in_pair.add(s)\n                used_in_pair.add(s_reverse)\n                seen_for_pairing.remove(s_reverse)\n            else:\n                seen_for_pairing.add(s)\n\n    return pair_count\n```"}
