{"task_id": "Mbpp/763", "solution": "```python\ndef find_min_diff(arr: tuple, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the minimum absolute difference between any two elements in the input array.\n    It sorts the array first, then finds the minimum difference among adjacent elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    arr_list = list(arr)\n    arr_list.sort()\n\n    min_diff = float('inf')\n\n    # Iterate through adjacent elements to find the minimum difference.\n    # This loop correctly handles arrays with n >= 2 elements.\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        current_diff = arr_list[i] - arr_list[i-1]\n        if current_diff < min_diff:\n            min_diff = current_diff\n\n    return int(min_diff)\n```"}
