{"task_id": "Mbpp/767", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\ndef get_pairs_count(numbers: List[Union[int, float]], target_sum: Union[int, float]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts pairs in a list that sum to the target_sum, handling duplicate numbers distinctly.\n    Uses a frequency map to achieve efficient O(N) average time complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    pair_count = 0\n    # Stores the frequency of numbers encountered so far.\n    freq_map = {}\n\n    for num in numbers:\n        complement = target_sum - num\n        # If the complement exists in the map, it means we found a pair.\n        if complement in freq_map:\n            pair_count += freq_map[complement]\n\n        # Increment the frequency of the current number.\n        freq_map[num] = freq_map.get(num, 0) + 1\n\n    return pair_count\n```"}
