{"task_id": "Mbpp/771", "solution": "```python\ndef check_expression(expression: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the given expression has balanced brackets, parentheses, and braces.\n    It uses a stack to track and match opening and closing symbols.\"\"\"\n    stack = []\n    mapping = {\")\": \"(\", \"]\": \"[\", \"}\": \"{\"}\n\n    for char in expression:\n        if char in mapping.values():  # If it's an opening bracket\n            stack.append(char)\n        elif char in mapping:  # If it's a closing bracket\n            if not stack or mapping[char] != stack.pop():\n                return False  # Mismatch or no opening bracket found\n\n    return not stack  # True if stack is empty (all matched), False otherwise\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/771", "solution": "def check_expression(expression_string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given expression string has balanced and correctly ordered delimiters.\n    Uses a stack-based approach to match opening and closing delimiters.\n    \"\"\"\n    stack = []\n\n    # Define delimiter mappings internally for self-containment\n    OPENING_DELIMITERS = {'(', '[', '{'}\n    CLOSING_DELIMITERS = {')', ']', '}'}\n    DELIMITER_PAIRS = {\n        ')': '(',\n        ']': '[',\n        '}': '{'\n    }\n\n    for char in expression_string:\n        if char in OPENING_DELIMITERS:\n            stack.append(char)\n        elif char in CLOSING_DELIMITERS:\n            if not stack:\n                return False  # Unmatched closing delimiter\n\n            last_open = stack.pop()\n            if DELIMITER_PAIRS[char] != last_open:\n                return False  # Mismatched opening and closing delimiters\n\n    return not stack # True if stack is empty (all matched), False otherwise (unmatched opening)"}
