{"task_id": "Mbpp/780", "solution": "```python\ndef find_combinations(input_list_of_tuples: list[tuple]) -> list[tuple]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes all unique element-wise sums of distinct tuple pairs from the input list.\n    Returns a list of these unique summed tuples.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(input_list_of_tuples) < 2:\n        return []\n\n    unique_summed_tuples = set()\n    num_tuples = len(input_list_of_tuples)\n\n    for i in range(num_tuples):\n        for j in range(i + 1, num_tuples):\n            tuple1 = input_list_of_tuples[i]\n            tuple2 = input_list_of_tuples[j]\n\n            # Perform element-wise summation\n            summed_tuple = tuple(x + y for x, y in zip(tuple1, tuple2))\n            unique_summed_tuples.add(summed_tuple)\n\n    return list(unique_summed_tuples)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/778", "solution": "```python\ndef pack_consecutive_duplicates(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Packs consecutive duplicate elements from input_list into sublists.\n    This groups contiguous identical items, including single elements in their own sublists.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    result_list = []\n    current_group = [input_list[0]]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(input_list)):\n        if input_list[i] == current_group[0]:\n            current_group.append(input_list[i])\n        else:\n            result_list.append(current_group)\n            current_group = [input_list[i]]\n\n    # Append the last group after the loop finishes\n    if current_group:\n        result_list.append(current_group)\n\n    return result_list\n```"}
