{"task_id": "Mbpp/797", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_in_range(l: int, r: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all odd natural numbers within the inclusive range [l, r].\n    The iteration starts from max(1, l) to ensure only natural numbers are considered.\n    \"\"\"\n    current_sum = 0\n    start = max(1, l)\n\n    for num in range(start, r + 1):\n        if num % 2 != 0:\n            current_sum += num\n\n    return current_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/797", "solution": "def _is_natural(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number is a natural number (positive integer).\"\"\"\n    return num >= 1\n\ndef _is_odd(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number is an odd integer.\"\"\"\n    return num % 2 != 0\n\ndef sum_in_range(l: int, r: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all odd natural numbers within the inclusive range [l, r].\"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    # Ensure iteration starts from at least 1, as natural numbers are positive.\n    effective_l = max(1, l)\n\n    for num in range(effective_l, r + 1):\n        if _is_natural(num) and _is_odd(num):\n            total_sum += num\n    return total_sum"}
