{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "```python\ndef left_rotate(number: int, bits_to_rotate: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Rotates a 32-bit integer left by a specified number of bits.\n    The result is masked to ensure it remains within the 32-bit range.\n    \"\"\"\n    effective_shift = bits_to_rotate % 32\n    # Perform the left rotation using bitwise operations.\n    rotated_number = (number << effective_shift) | (number >> (32 - effective_shift))\n    # Mask the result to 32 bits to enforce the 32-bit constraint.\n    return rotated_number & 0xFFFFFFFF\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "def right_insertion(sorted_list: list, target_value: object) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the right insertion point for a specified value in a sorted list using binary search.\n    It returns the index where the value should be inserted to maintain sorted order.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(sorted_list)\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if target_value < sorted_list[mid]:\n            high = mid\n        else:\n            low = mid + 1\n    return low"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "```python\ndef left_rotate(number: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Performs a 32-bit left bitwise rotation on the given number by d bits.\n    Bits shifted off the left re-enter on the right.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Normalize the rotation amount to ensure it's within the 0-31 bit range.\n    d_normalized = d % 32\n\n    # Combine the left-shifted bits and the right-shifted (wrapped-around) bits, then apply a 32-bit mask.\n    return ((number << d_normalized) | (number >> (32 - d_normalized))) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n```"}
